OL,3,GNEWSAFarmer 'thankful to be alive'
OL,4,Aafter falling through roof at work
OL,5,
OL,6,FRichard Spence was working at his
OL,7,Ffamily farm when he fell through the
OL,8,Froof of a cow shed, breaking a number
OL,9,Fof ribs and bones in his back.
OL,11,FHe believes he is lucky to be alive,
OL,12,Fafter spending months in hospital and
OL,13,Fbeing diagnosed with a brain injury as
OL,14,Fa result of head injuries from the
OL,15,Ffall.
OL,17,FNow he is raising awareness of the
OL,18,Fdangers of working at heights,
OL,19,Femphasising that if someone gets
OL,20,Finjured, their family and friends are
OL,21,Fimpacted too, "so just take a minute,
OL,22,Fand don't take any risks".
OL,23,APub: 30-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
FL,415,410,260,120,0,100
